// BUG-959 (refactor L stage 2): a `break` inside a DEFER BODY's own loop.
//
// HONEST SCOPE — this test does NOT discriminate against any released compiler, and it
// is here anyway. Measured: it compiles and runs correctly on the pre-L build too. The
// abort it pins ("IR_DEFER_PUSH has no CFG-reachable IR_DEFER_FIRE") existed only in L's
// INTERMEDIATE third attempt, which never shipped — before the template machinery
// existed there was nothing to bake a stray fire into.
//
// What it IS: a pin on a shape that is legal (only since BUG-947), non-obvious, and
// interacts directly with the template machinery — so a future change to how a body is
// lowered or cloned can re-break it. Recorded because the diagnosis cost a full attempt:
// the break reached `emit_defer_fire_scoped`, which baked a stray IR_DEFER_FIRE INTO the
// template, and every fire then cloned it, leaving the real PUSH with no fire outside a
// body copy. Suppressing only the SPLICE was not enough — the INSTRUCTION is the half
// that breaks validation. `defer_body_depth > 0` now returns from all three fire
// emitters.
//
// The loop runs exactly twice before the break, so `g` ends at 2.

u32 g;

void f() {
    defer {
        for (u32 i = 0; i < 5; i += 1) {
            if (i == 2) { break; }
            g += 1;
        }
    }
}

u32 main() {
    f();
    if (g != 2) { return 1; }
    return 0;
}
